Z||000007||billfredmike24||08-17-2001||03:01 PM||||after experimenting with the wires, this is what happened. <P>Illumination wire from deck with the gray and brown wires brightened the lights in the instrument panel and the radio worked fine, but i could not dim any of the lights.<P>Illumination wire and brown, everthing worked but gray not attached and this is when the fuses blew before.  Also instrument panel is not as bright.<P>Illumination wire and gray, everything worked but instrument panel not that bright.<P>Leave the three wire disconnected, no lights on deck until it's turned on, instrument panel not very bright.<P>Any suggestions on how to have the instrument panels bright, (grey and brown together), Illumination on deck when it's not turned on (illumination wire and either grey or brown) and still be able to dim the lights(grey can't be touching brown)<P>Confusing i know but any ides?<BR>Thanks Mike <p>[This message has been edited by billfredmike24 (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
